Subject: [freebsd-ports PATCH v3] net-mgmt/signoz: Observability platform for
 logs, metrics, and traces
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:02:38 +0000

SigNoz is an open source observability platform. It brings logs,
metrics, and traces together in one application, with dashboards,
alerts, exceptions, and service maps. It is native to OpenTelemetry and
stores its data in ClickHouse.

This is the Community Edition of the query service and web interface.
Telemetry reaches ClickHouse through the SigNoz distribution of the
OpenTelemetry Collector, which is packaged separately.

WWW: https://signoz.io/
---
Notes for review:

Build: on a ports tree from today, the port fetches, builds, stages,
and passes check-plist with Go 1.27. STRICT_DEPENDS was set, and no
dependency was built. The staged binary starts, migrates its SQLite
store, and starts its HTTP server; with no ClickHouse it logs
connection errors, as expected. Not checked: a poudriere build,
aarch64, a run as the signoz user from rc.d (that needs root), and a
request to the web interface (the sandbox here refused connections to
the port).

sonic: signoz v0.145.0 pins github.com/bytedance/sonic v1.14.1. Its
map code is limited to Go 1.24 and 1.25, so it does not compile with
the tree's Go 1.26 or 1.27. The port raises sonic to v1.15.4 and
sonic/loader to v0.5.2, the only modules "go get" moves; tidy then
adds bytedance/gopkg v0.1.3. go.mk downloads modules in go-post-fetch
and vendors them in go-post-extract, both at priority 800, so a patch
to go.mod comes too late. post-fetch and post-extract run at 700 and
apply the same "go mod edit" first. The edit in DIST_SUBDIR makes
go-post-fetch download the bumped modules while the network is up; the
edit in WRKSRC makes go-post-extract vendor them. With the network
blocked, the tidy and vendor steps of extract still succeed.

mmap: sonic/loader v0.5.2 maps memory with MAP_ANON and fd 0.
FreeBSD requires fd -1 and returns EINVAL, so the built binary
panicked at startup. The vendor patch passes -1. Upstream made the
same fix in bytedance/sonic commit bf12ab8, merged on 2026-09-26, and
the patch header cites it. No sonic or loader release includes it
yet, so the patch stays until signoz requires a loader release that
does.

Active query log: the PromQL engine keeps queries.active in
prometheus.active_query_tracker.path, which defaults to "", the
working directory. Under rc.d that is /, which the signoz user cannot
write, so the engine panics. I reproduced this by starting the binary
from / as an unprivileged user. post-patch points the default at
/var/db/signoz in the source and in example.yaml.

Makefile, line by line:
- MASTER_SITES and DISTFILES (:web): the web interface comes prebuilt
  from upstream's release tarball, since the pnpm build has no offline
  path in the tree. The source maps are left out because they make up
  31 MB of its 54 MB and only browser developer tools read them.
- LICENSE_FILE: installs upstream's license with the package.
- ONLY_FOR_ARCHS: upstream releases only amd64 and arm64.
  modernc.org/sqlite has no FreeBSD support on powerpc64 or riscv64.
- GO_BUILDFLAGS: variant and version appear in "signoz -v" and the
  startup log. "-s -w" is dropped because INSTALL_PROGRAM already
  strips the binary.
- SUB_FILES: pkg-message names %%DATADIR%%.
- USERS and GROUPS: rc.d runs signoz as this user, which owns
  /var/db/signoz.
- SONIC_BUMP: one value for both edits, so the two cannot drift.

UIDs/GIDs: signoz takes 485, beside prometheus 478, alertmanager 479,
and promxy 481.

Changes in v3:
- Cite upstream's mmap fix in the vendor patch header.
